  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "ESCALATE",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "Both sides have run the arithmetic the same way, and I agree with it. The GPS trace for trip TRP-02859 covers the whole journey at a 10-second interval with no gaps, and it records 92.0 km driven — the governing figure under POL-RD-01 — against a booking-time optimal route of 22.0 km. That is an excess of 70.0 km, 318% of optimal, which clears both POL-RD-01 establishment tests (over 20% and over 0.8 km) and both materiality tests (over 50% and over 8.0 km), so the deviation is established AND material. The meter's 138.8 minutes against a 30.0-minute optimal is consistent with the same trace.\n\nNothing on the record excuses any of it. The chat log for this trip holds zero messages, so there was no rider-requested detour and POL-RD-04 cannot run — no distance is excluded. No pickup or dropoff was amended (both amendment timestamps and amended_optimal_distance_km are null), so POL-RD-05 gives no adjusted comparator. This is a metered RYDE_X trip, not pooled and not upfront-quoted, so POL-RD-11 and POL-RD-12 do not apply. The only traffic advisory in the bundle, EV-ADVIS-02859-01, is MISSING at weight 0.0, so no closure can be shown and POL-RD-03 is unavailable (POL-RD-13). The driver's statement that the rider 'was unresponsive and gave no destination' cites no evidence ID, names no waypoint and identifies no advisory; under POL-RD-08 it carries no weight, and POL-RD-14 does not apply because there was no instruction for the trace to corroborate.\n\nThe refund is then arithmetic under POL-RD-02: (base fare 3.80 + 0.75 x 22.0 km + 0.28 x 30.0 min) x the 2.0 surge multiplier read from the fare breakdown = 28.70 x 2.0 = 57.40, plus the 0.80 platform fee = a recomputed fare of 58.20. The charged total was 224.12, so the refund is 224.12 - 58.20 = 165.92, which rounds up to 165.95. It is 74.0% of the charge, below the 90% share that would convert it to a full refund, so on its own it would be a partial refund. No ERP, toll or surcharge line is added on top, because the fare carries none and the trip did not originate at an airport (POL-RD-09).\n\nThat refund of 165.92 exceeds the SGD 150.00 ceiling in POL-RD-10(6). That trigger is mandatory and terminal under POL-GEN-03: I cannot issue the money myself. The case goes to a human reviewer with the full file, no money moves, and the disputed amount is held rather than refunded. The reviewer's question is whether to release the POL-RD-02 refund of 165.95 or vary it; the record is otherwise complete and no further evidence is needed. No referral is made: the driver's POL-RD-06 check is clean (deviation_flags_90d of 0 over completed_trips_90d of 300, so no pattern is established), and there is no phantom billing line to refer under POL-RD-09(4). The rider's profile likewise attracts no corroboration add-on under POL-RD-08. Confidence is 0.95, drawn from the fare breakdown, trip record and GPS trace, all at full weight and none impaired."
  },
