    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "Both of you should see where this lands and why. The measurement is not in dispute. For trip TRP-02859 the GPS trace runs 92.0 km against a booking-time optimal route of 22.0 km — an excess of 70.0 km, or 318.18% of optimal — so under POL-RD-01 the deviation is ESTABLISHED and MATERIAL, and the trace that carries it is unimpaired for policy purposes under POL-RD-07 (834 fixes at a 10-second interval, 100.0% coverage, no gaps, maximum gap 0.0 s), so nothing about a broken trace changes the picture and the rider's initial burden under POL-RD-08 is met. No clause excuses the excess: the chat log holds zero messages, so there is no rider-requested detour for POL-RD-04 to act on; pickup_amended_at and dropoff_amended_at are both null, so POL-RD-05 changes no comparator; and the only traffic advisory in the bundle (EV-ADVIS-02859-01) is admissibility-MISSING at weight 0.0 with issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, so POL-RD-03 cannot be run and any 'traffic was bad' explanation carries no weight under POL-RD-13 and POL-RD-08. The driver's statement that the rider was unresponsive cites no evidence ID and does not satisfy POL-RD-04(a)–(c). The POL-RD-06 check on the driver comes back clean — deviation_flags_90d is 0 against completed_trips_90d of 300 — so no pattern is established and neither the uplift nor a conduct referral follows.\n\nOn the arithmetic the rider asked for: the fare is METERED and the surge multiplier of 2.0 is read from the fare_breakdown (not the trip_record). POL-RD-02 gives recomputed_fare = ((3.80 + 0.75 × 22.0 + 0.28 × 30.0) × 2.0) + 0.80 = (28.70 × 2.0) + 0.80 = 58.20. Charged_total is 224.12, so the refund would be 224.12 − 58.20 = 165.92, rounded up to SGD 165.95. That is 74.03% of charged_total, below the 90% share that would convert it to a full refund, and there are no ERP or surcharge lines for POL-RD-09 to add on top.\n\nThat refund figure is why no money moves today. POL-RD-10(6) makes a computed POL-RD-02 refund above SGD 150.00 a mandatory escalation, and 165.92 exceeds it. I am therefore not permitted to issue the monetary ruling either side's arithmetic points to: the ruling is ESCALATE, it is terminal and it replaces any money outcome, and the SGD 116.50 in dispute is held rather than collected or refunded. No clause produces a referral here (POL-RD-06(c) does not fire, and there is no POL-RD-09(4) phantom or misapplied line), so the referrals list is empty. The human reviewer receives the deviation finding, the 165.92 computation and the missing advisory. The open question for that reviewer, which belongs here rather than in a referral, is whether the escalation ceiling is meant to catch a refund of this size or whether the comparator route should be adjusted — nothing on this record adjusts it, and no advisory, chat instruction or amendment is available to do so."
  },
